{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"426\t/**\n427\t * Convert a line that is not a `user`/`assistant` turn into the record it\n428\t * deserves, or return null when the type is genuinely unknown (the caller\n429\t * then routes it to the drift path).\n430\t *\n431\t * `system` lines split on whether they carry text. Claude Code uses the type\n432\t * for two unrelated things: printing into the conversation (a slash command's\n433\t * stdout, an away summary, a refusal fallback — all of which the user read,\n434\t * so they are turns spoken by the system) and recording harness bookkeeping\n435\t * (turn durations, hook summaries — which nobody read, so they are activity).\n436\t * A string `content` field is exactly the difference, so that is the test,\n437\t * rather than a subtype list that would go stale the moment Claude Code adds\n438\t * a subtype.\n439\t */\n440\tfunction convertRecordLine(line: ClaudeTranscriptLine, ctx: RecordContext): EventDraft | null {\n441\t  const type = line.type;\n442\t  if (typeof type !== \"string\") return null;\n443\t  const fields = payloadFields(line as unknown as Record<string, unknown>);\n444\t\n445\t  if (type === \"system\") {\n446\t    if (typeof line.content === \"string\" && line.content.trim() !== \"\") {\n447\t      return recordDraft(\n448\t        ctx,\n449\t        \"conversation_turn\",\n450\t        \"system\",\n451\t        { ...liftText(fields, \"content\"), role: \"system\" },\n452\t        line,\n453\t      );\n454\t    }\n455\t    return activityDraft(ctx, `system/${line.subtype ?? \"untyped\"}`, fields, line);\n456\t  }\n457\t\n458\t  if (type === \"attachment\") {\n459\t    const attachmentType = line.attachment?.type;\n460\t    return contextInjectionDraft(\n461\t      ctx,\n462\t      `attachment/${typeof attachmentType === \"string\" ? attachmentType : \"untyped\"}`,\n463\t      fields,\n464\t      line,\n465\t    );\n466\t  }\n467\t\n468\t  if (SESSION_STATE_LINE_TYPES.has(type)) {\n469\t    return sessionStateDraft(ctx, type, fields, line);\n470\t  }\n471\t\n472\t  if (ACTIVITY_LINE_TYPES.has(type)) {\n473\t    // A `queue-operation` enqueue carries the queued prompt or task\n474\t    // notification verbatim — the one activity type that is mostly text.\n475\t    return activityDraft(ctx, type, liftText(fields, \"content\"), line);\n476\t  }\n477\t\n478\t  return null;\n479\t}\n480\t\n481\t/** Raw-only preservation event for an unrecognized claude-code line (see drift.ts). */\n482\tfunction preserve(\n483\t  type: string,\n484\t  line: ClaudeTranscriptLine,\n485\t  occurredAt: string,\n486\t  seq: number,\n487\t  fileSessionId: string,\n488\t  version: string,\n489\t): EventDraft {\n490\t  const sessionId = line.sessionId ?? fileSessionId;\n491\t  const conversation = conversationFor(line, sessionId);\n492\t  return unrecognizedDraft({\n493\t    typeKey: type,\n494\t    line,\n495\t    occurredAt,\n496\t    source: \"claude-code\",\n497\t    sessionId,\n498\t    seq,\n499\t    version,\n500\t    rawFormat: RAW_FORMAT,\n501\t    conversationId: conversation.id,\n502\t    ...(conversation.parent ? { parentConversationId: conversation.parent } : {}),\n503\t    agent: agentContext(line),\n504\t  });\n505\t}\n506\t\n507\t/**\n508\t * The `RecordContext` a non-turn line converts under. Split out so the\n509\t * capture loop and the re-normalization hook build it identically — the\n510\t * context feeds `conversation` and `occurred_at`, both of which are part of\n511\t * event identity, so any divergence between the two paths would mint a second\n512\t * copy of an event instead of deduping against the first.\n513\t */\n514\tfunction recordContext(\n515\t  line: ClaudeTranscriptLine,\n516\t  occurredAt: string,\n517\t  seq: number,\n518\t  fileSessionId: string,\n519\t  version: string,\n520\t): RecordContext {\n521\t  const sessionId = line.sessionId ?? fileSessionId;\n522\t  const conversation = conversationFor(line, sessionId);\n523\t  return {\n524\t    occurredAt,\n525\t    source: \"claude-code\",\n526\t    sessionId,\n527\t    seq,\n528\t    version,\n529\t    rawFormat: RAW_FORMAT,\n530\t    conversationId: conversation.id,\n531\t    ...(conversation.parent ? { parentConversationId: conversation.parent } : {}),\n532\t    agent: agentContext(line),\n533\t  };\n534\t}\n535\t\n536\t/**\n537\t * A `user`/`assistant` line, as a turn.\n538\t *\n539\t * Sidechain lines convert here now rather than being dropped: they are the\n540\t * subagent's side of the conversation, and the only reason to skip them was\n541\t * that the ledger had no way to say whose subagent they were. `conversationFor`\n542\t * gives them one. The subagent *type* Claude Code attributes an assistant\n543\t * sidechain line to (`attributionAgent`, e.g. \"Explore\") goes in `content`\n544\t * beside `role`, where opencode's agent persona already lives — it describes\n545\t * which agent spoke, which `producer` (the capture tool and the model) has no","tool_use_id":"toolu_01KGnUZsEcJohPVEFQhZx1Yo","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"0efe101ae3a794ff333e1c5b4122fdb71b3266fd","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:8f1a9339-b2b4-4bad-b2a9-3123e47d2a77","seq":878},"id":"ev1-fa2c415d1a2ae030a806940091cd0b8b42b7cfe29cf0025b1e8ffa0f4378d7a9","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-06T01:24:37.622Z","producer":{"session_id":"8f1a9339-b2b4-4bad-b2a9-3123e47d2a77","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.223","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":