{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"commit 0efe101ae3a794ff333e1c5b4122fdb71b3266fd\nAuthor: Evin Tunador <evintunador@gmail.com>\nDate:   Wed Aug 5 21:42:37 2026 -0400\n\n    0.20.0: Gemini CLI and Qwen Code adapters\n    \n    Adds capture for the two CLIs at the top of the roadmap's TODO list, rebased\n    onto 0.19.0 and built to its bar: no skip lists, every record gets a kind.\n    \n    Gemini CLI (`~/.gemini/tmp/<project>/chats/session-*.jsonl`) is the harder of\n    the two: the file is append-only but is a write-ahead log of mutations to one\n    conversation document, not a transcript. Capture replays it with Gemini's own\n    record precedence, but deliberately does not honour its removals — verified on\n    a live session, Gemini rewrote the document after a failed API call and\n    silently dropped the prompt the user had just typed. The ledger keeps the\n    union of every message the file ever held, each at its last-written value, and\n    records the `$rewindTo` itself as an `activity` naming what it withdrew, so a\n    withdrawn turn is legible as withdrawn rather than merely present. `$set`\n    patches become `session_state`; `info`/`error`/`warning` notices become turns\n    spoken by the system. Because nothing is removed, `seq` is assigned at first\n    sighting over messages and mutations alike and never reused, so a rewind\n    cannot renumber later turns. Sub-sessions under `<chats>/<parent id>/` are\n    captured as sub-conversations.\n    \n    Qwen Code (`~/.qwen/projects/<escaped-cwd>/chats/<id>.jsonl`) forked Gemini CLI\n    but not its store: plain append-only JSONL with a claude-code-shaped envelope,\n    so the adapter is that adapter's twin — per-line conversion, line-index `seq`,\n    a torn-tail-safe cursor, the same catch-up sweep. Everything that is not a turn\n    arrives as a `system` line discriminated by `subtype`: `attribution_snapshot`\n    becomes `file_snapshot` (per-file content hashes are in the record itself, so\n    nothing needs resolving against a local cache), the title/source/goal subtypes\n    become `session_state`, `at_command` and the agent-launch prompts become\n    `context_injection`, and everything else becomes `activity` rather than being\n    dropped. A `parent_session` record makes a subagent chat a sub-conversation.\n    \n    Both CLIs express content as Google GenAI `Part` lists, so that conversion is\n    shared in genai-parts.ts.\n    \n    Also:\n    - Extracts the cursor into adapters/common.ts and puts all five adapters on\n      it. 0.19.0 taught the claude-code cursor three things the others still did\n      not know — absent is not zero, `size` bounds the sweep, the write must be\n      atomic — and the fix for each was worth having everywhere rather than in one\n      of five copies.\n    - Fixes the torn-trailing-line bug in codex, which 0.19.0 fixed for\n      claude-code only: the cursor advanced past a half-written line, so the\n      completed line was never captured. Uses the same narrow rule (unterminated\n      file *and* final line), because holding at any parse failure would stall a\n      session's capture forever on real corruption.\n    - `cledger capture <gemini-cli|qwen-code> --all` backfills every session the\n      CLI scopes to this directory; the hook's own sweep is deliberately narrower\n      and only finishes sessions cledger already tracks.\n    \n    Verified end to end against live CLIs: `cledger install qwen-code` followed by\n    a real `qwen` run captures the session automatically — 6 turns, 2 file\n    snapshots and 5 activity records, with the machinery kinds correctly hidden\n    from the default `log` view.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ewo7xu7kzLpH4MeEDK5LDc\n\ndiff --git a/src/adapters/codex.ts b/src/adapters/codex.ts\nindex 062423d..8259288 100644\n--- a/src/adapters/codex.ts\n+++ b/src/adapters/codex.ts\n@@ -1,9 +1,9 @@\n-import { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n-import { mkdir, readFile, stat, writeFile } from \"node:fs/promises\";\n-import { basename, join } from \"node:path\";\n-import { findRepo, gitUserIdentity, type GitUserIdentity, type RepoInfo } from \"../git.js\";\n+import { readFile, stat } from \"node:fs/promises\";\n+import { basename } from \"node:path\";\n+import { findRepo, gitUserIdentity, type GitUserIdentity } from \"../git.js\";\n import { appendEvents } from \"../store.js\";\n import type { Actor, EventDraft, EvidenceEvent, ProducerAgentContext } from \"../schema.js\";\n+import { packageVersion, readCursor, writeCursor } from \"./common.js\";\n import {\n   countUnrecognized,\n   reasoningDraft,\n@@ -20,6 +20,8 @@ import {\n \n const RAW_FORMAT = \"codex-rollout-jsonl/2\";\n \n+const CURSOR_FIELD = \"lines\";\n+\n /** Codex CLI hooks-engine payload (subset we read). */\n interface CodexHookPayload {\n   session_id?: string;\n@@ -185,41 +187,6 @@ function initialAgentContext(lines: string[], cursor: number): CodexAgentState {\n   return state;\n }\n \n-function packageVersion(): string {\n-  try {\n-    const pkg = JSON.parse(\n-      readFileSync(new URL(\"../../package.json\", import.meta.url), \"utf8\"),\n-    ) as { version?: string };\n-    return pkg.version ?? \"0.1.0\";\n-  } catch {\n-    return \"0.1.0\";\n-  }\n-}\n-\n-function sanitizeId(id: string): string {\n-  return id.replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_-]/g, \"_\");\n-}\n-\n-function cursorPath(repo: RepoInfo, sessionId: string): string {\n-  return join(repo.commonDir, \"conversation-ledger\", \"cursors\", `${sanitizeId(sessionId)}.json`);\n-}\n-\n-async function readCursor(repo: RepoInfo, sessionId: string): Promise<number> {\n-  try {\n-    const raw = await readFile(cursorPath(repo, sessionId), \"utf8\");\n-    const data = JSON.parse(raw) as { lines?: number };\n-    return typeof data.lines === \"number\" ? data.lines : 0;\n-  } catch {\n-    return 0;\n-  }\n-}\n-\n-async function writeCursor(repo: RepoInfo, sessionId: string, lines: number): Promise<void> {\n-  const path = cursorPath(repo, sessionId);\n-  await mkdir(join(repo.commonDir, \"conversation-ledger\", \"cursors\"), { recursive: true });\n-  await writeFile(path, JSON.stringify({ lines }) + \"\\n\");\n-}\n-\n /** Extract the trailing uuid from `rollout-<ts>-<uuid>.jsonl`, else the bare filename. */\n function sessionIdFromFilename(transcriptPath: string): string {\n   const name = basename(transcriptPath, \".jsonl\");\n@@ -572,6 +539,10 @@ export async function captureCodexTranscript(\n   } catch {\n     return result; // transcript not written yet\n   }\n+  // Whether the writer had finished the last line when we read. A rollout that\n+  // does not end in a newline was caught mid-write, which is how the final\n+  // line comes to be torn — see `tornTail` below.\n+  const endsWithNewline = raw.endsWith(\"\\n\");\n   const lines = raw.split(\"\\n\");\n   if (lines.length > 0 && lines[lines.length - 1] === \"\") lines.pop();\n \n@@ -586,13 +557,22 @@ export async function captureCodexTranscript(\n     }\n   }\n \n-  let cursor = await readCursor(repo, sessionId);\n+  let cursor = (await readCursor(repo, sessionId, CURSOR_FIELD))?.count ?? 0;\n   if (cursor > lines.length) cursor = 0; // transcript is shorter than expected — rescan from the start\n \n   const baseTime = await sessionBaseTime(transcriptPath);\n   const version = packageVersion();\n   const identity = await gitUserIdentity(repo);\n   const agent = initialAgentContext(lines, cursor);\n+  /**\n+   * Index of a half-written final line, when there is one. Advancing the\n+   * cursor past it would skip that line permanently once the bytes land;\n+   * holding the cursor short of it means the next capture reads it whole.\n+   * Both conditions are load-bearing: a parse failure anywhere but the\n+   * unterminated last line is real corruption, and stopping there would stall\n+   * this session's capture forever.","is_error":false,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NYEiVfCA4TRafYwbuQt5iN","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"0efe101ae3a794ff333e1c5b4122fdb71b3266fd","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:d10310cd-8144-4046-87b9-97bbb6ace18c","seq":155},"id":"ev1-a09377fab59a7e5fa332e9c2f1e83f20679ca06775b260285a958b716b42d4e9","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-06T04:41:03.039Z","producer":{"session_id":"d10310cd-8144-4046-87b9-97bbb6ace18c","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.223","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"commit 0efe101ae3a794ff333e1c5b4122fdb71b3266fd\nAuthor: Evin Tunador <evintunador@gmail.com>\nDate:   Wed Aug 5 21:42:37 2026 -0400\n\n    0.20.0: Gemini CLI and Qwen Code adapters\n    \n    Adds capture for the two CLIs at the top of the roadmap's TODO list, rebased\n    onto 0.19.0 and built to its bar: no skip lists, every record gets a kind.\n    \n    Gemini CLI (`~/.gemini/tmp/<project>/chats/session-*.jsonl`) is the harder of\n    the two: the file is append-only but is a write-ahead log of mutations to one\n    conversation document, not a transcript. Capture replays it with Gemini's own\n    record precedence, but deliberately does not honour its removals — verified on\n    a live session, Gemini rewrote the document after a failed API call and\n    silently dropped the prompt the user had just typed. The ledger keeps the\n    union of every message the file ever held, each at its last-written value, and\n    records the `$rewindTo` itself as an `acti