{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_0165dhxEBG3rt9iGQ4oE13kt","input":{"content":"---\nname: project-cledger-gemini-qwen-adapters\ndescription: \"gemini-cli + qwen-code adapters, 0.20.0 (PR #5); rebased onto 0.19.0's full-capture bar; gemini WAL union-capture + rewind-as-activity, shared cursor, codex torn-line fix\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n---\n\nAdapters for Gemini CLI and Qwen Code, 0.20.0, PR #5 (branch\n`worktree-more-cli-adapters`). **Rebased onto 0.19.0 after PR #4 merged**\n(2026-08-06) and rewritten to its bar — the earlier conflict is resolved and\nthe PR is MERGEABLE.\n\nBoth CLIs were npm-installed globally and driven against the local ds4-gateway\n(`http://127.0.0.1:9002/v1`, OpenAI-compatible, model `deepseek-v4-flash`) to\nproduce real sessions — that endpoint is the cheap way to generate real\ntranscripts for any OpenAI-compatible CLI without accounts. Gemini CLI does\n*not* accept an OpenAI base URL; its format was pinned from its shipped\n(unminified) bundle at\n`/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/@google/gemini-cli/bundle/`. Qwen's authoritative\n`RECORD_TYPES` / `KNOWN_RECORD_SUBTYPES` sets live in its own bundle too.\n\nDecisions worth remembering:\n\n- **Gemini's session file is a write-ahead log, not a transcript.** Records:\n  `$rewindTo` removal, bare message upsert by durable id, `$set` metadata patch\n  (a `$set.messages` array replaces the whole document), and the\n  `sessionId`+`projectHash` header. Verified: after a failed API call Gemini\n  wrote a snapshot that dropped the prompt the user had just typed. So capture\n  takes the **union** of every message ever written (last value wins) rather\n  than replaying removals. With 0.19.0's `activity` kind the `$rewindTo` is now\n  recorded itself, naming what it withdrew — the roadmap gap from the first\n  version of the PR is closed.\n- **Gemini `seq` spans messages *and* mutation records** in one first-sighting\n  number space, so the two can't collide and a rewind can't renumber.\n- **Qwen routes everything non-turn through `system` + `subtype`**;\n  `attribution_snapshot` → `file_snapshot` (content hashes are in the record,\n  so `resolved` stays empty), title/source/goal → `session_state`, at-command\n  and agent-launch prompts → `context_injection`, all else → `activity`.\n  `parent_session` gives the sub-conversation link.\n- **Shared cursor in `adapters/common.ts`**, all five adapters on it. 0.19.0's\n  claude-code cursor knew three things the others didn't: absent≠zero (gates\n  the sweep), `size` bounds the sweep, atomic write (two writers). Field names\n  preserved per adapter so nothing on disk resets.\n- **Codex still had the torn-trailing-line bug** 0.19.0 fixed only for\n  claude-code; fixed here with the same narrow rule (unterminated file *and*\n  final line — holding at any parse failure stalls capture forever on real\n  corruption).\n- **Qwen headless mode kills hooks.** `qwen -p` fires `Stop` then exits,\n  tearing down the hook process. Fix: `install` appends `>/dev/null 2>&1`,\n  which reliably works but costs visible drift warnings. Same trade the\n  opencode plugin makes.\n\nKnown gaps left in the Roadmap: Gemini stamps no CLI version into its session\nfile (no `producer.source_version`), and Qwen subtypes are classified by name\nrather than observed shape (wrong *kind* possible, never lost content).\n\nSee [[project-cledger-full-capture]] for the 0.19.0 bar this was rebuilt onto,\nand [[project-cledger-opencode-adapter]] for the adapter conventions all five\nfollow.\n","file_path":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/memory/project-cledger-gemini-qwen-adapters.md"},"name":"Write","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"0efe1