{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Sanity check before wrapping: full suite green (188 pass, 1 pre-existing skip), typecheck clean with no unused locals, `dist/` untracked, and the live end-to-end run captured a real Qwen session through the installed hook.\n\n**Draft PR #5: https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/5** (branch `worktree-more-cli-adapters`, 16 files)\n\nTwo new adapters, both verified against live CLIs rather than guessed — I installed `@google/gemini-cli` and `@qwen-code/qwen-code` globally and drove Qwen against your local ds4-gateway to get real transcripts, so no accounts were needed.\n\n**Qwen Code** turned out easy: plain append-only JSONL with a claude-code-shaped envelope, so its adapter is that adapter's twin.\n\n**Gemini CLI** was the interesting one. Its session file is append-only but is a *write-ahead log of mutations*, not a transcript. The important find: on a real session, after a failed API call Gemini rewrote the document with a snapshot that **silently dropped the prompt I had just typed**. Replaying it faithfully — what Gemini itself does — would record no trace of that prompt ever being asked. Given this project exists to record everything, I made capture keep the union of every message the file ever held, treating rewinds as facts about Gemini's live view rather than instructions to forget. That also made `seq` strictly better than opencode's: assigned at first sighting, never reused, so a rewind can't renumber later turns.\n\nBoth CLIs express content as Google GenAI `Part` lists, so that conversion lives once in a shared module.\n\n**A bug I found and fixed along the way:** the existing claude-code and codex adapters advanced their cursor past a half-written trailing line, so the completed line was never captured — a silent, permanent loss of one turn whenever a hook fired mid-write. Fixed in all three, with a test.\n\n**One thing you should know about:** `install` appends `>/dev/null 2>&1` to the hook command for these two CLIs. `qwen -p` fires its Stop hook and immediately exits, killing the hook process; a slow probe hook reproduced it every time. The redirection fixes it reliably, but the capture no longer prints drift warnings where you can see them — same trade the opencode plugin already makes. It's documented in the Roadmap as an upstream fix.\n\nAlso worth flagging: **PR #4 (`worktree-capture-everything`, 0.19.0) overlaps this one** — it touches the same three existing adapters and removes the skip lists that this PR adds two more of. Whichever merges second needs a rebase. I took 0.20.0 to avoid the version collision.\n\nYour `~/.qwen/settings.json` and `~/.gemini/settings.json` now have the hooks installed; they'll no-op until this merges and you relink, since the global `cledger` still points at your main checkout at 0.18.0.\n\nI did not attempt Kimi CLI (already installed on your machine, `~/.kimi-code/`) — its `wire.jsonl` store looked promising but every session on disk was empty, and driving it needs a provider registry set up. I updated its README entry with what I learned about its layout so it's ready to pick up next.\n\nresult: Draft PR #5 adds verified Gemini CLI + Qwen Code capture adapters to conversation-ledger (0.20.0), plus a fix for a torn-trailing-line bug that silently dropped turns in the existing claude-code and codex adapters.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"0efe101ae3a794ff333e1c5b4122fdb71b3266fd","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:8f1a9339-b2b4-4bad-b2a9-3123e47d2a77","seq":815},"id":"ev1-a106a2cddefa22596ad1667459ed0306c4fb5869b5e681c9b1747aa520688afd","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-04T04:51:56.145Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"8f1a9339-