{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Sanity check: full suite green (196 pass, 1 pre-existing skip), typecheck clean with no unused locals, GitHub reports the PR `MERGEABLE`, and a live `qwen` run through the installed hook captured turns plus the new record kinds.\n\n**PR #5 rebased and updated: https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/5**\n\nI rebased onto your merged 0.19.0 rather than merging — both PRs rewrote the same adapters, so a textual merge would have been guesswork. The conflicts are gone.\n\nOn bringing the new CLIs up to #4's bar, the skip lists are gone from both:\n\n**Qwen** funnels everything non-turn through `system` + `subtype`, so I routed by subtype using its own `RECORD_TYPES`/`KNOWN_RECORD_SUBTYPES` lists read out of its bundle. `attribution_snapshot` → `file_snapshot` (and unlike Claude Code's file history, the per-file content hashes are already *in* the record, so nothing needs resolving against a local cache), title/source/goal → `session_state`, at-command and agent-launch prompts → `context_injection`, everything else → `activity`. Its `parent_session` record gives real sub-conversation links. Re-capturing my real sessions now yields 46 turns, 52 activity and 20 file_snapshot events with nothing dropped.\n\n**Gemini** got the bigger win. Last time I had to file \"a rewind is recorded only by its consequences\" as a roadmap item because there was no kind that fit. `activity` fits, so `$rewindTo` is now its own event naming the messages it withdrew — a withdrawn turn is finally legible as withdrawn rather than just present. `$set` patches became `session_state`, and the `info`/`error`/`warning` notices I'd skipped became turns spoken by the system. I also extended `seq` to span messages *and* mutation records in one first-sighting number space, and added sub-session capture from `<chats>/<parent id>/`.\n\nTwo things I found while doing it, which go beyond what you asked:\n\n- **Codex still had the torn-trailing-line bug** — #4 fixed it for claude-code only. The cursor advanced past a half-written line, so the completed line was never captured. Fixed with your narrower rule (unterminated file *and* final line), not my original broader one, which would stall capture forever on real mid-file corruption.\n- **The cursor moved into `adapters/common.ts` and all five adapters use it.** #4 taught the claude-code cursor three things the others didn't know — absent≠zero, `size` bounds the sweep, the write must be atomic — and each was worth having everywhere rather than in one of five copies. Field names are preserved per adapter, so no cursor on disk resets.\n\nVerified end to end: a live `qwen` run editing a file captured 6 turns, 2 file snapshots and 5 activity records through the installed hook, with the machinery kinds correctly hidden from the default `log` view.\n\nTwo gaps I left in the Roadmap rather than papering over: Gemini stamps no CLI version into its session file, so those events have no `producer.source_version` (reading it off the installed binary would be wrong for a backfill); and Qwen's subtypes are classified by name from its own list, since only two appear in the sessions I have — fields pass through verbatim either way, so the risk is a record under a slightly wrong kind, not lost content.\n\nThe only CI check is GitGuardian, still pending.\n\nresult: PR #5 rebased onto merged 0.19.0 and now MERGEABLE — Gemini CLI and Qwen Code adapters rebuilt to the full-capture bar (session_state/activity/context_injection/file_snapshot, sub-conversations, rewinds as events), plus a shared cursor and a codex torn-line fix.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"0efe101ae3a794ff333e1c5b4122fdb71b3266fd","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-c